# --- Secrets and local environment (never commit; see .env.example) ---
.env
.env.deploy
# Any backup of any .env — each carries the same live credentials as the file
# it copied. One glob covers the whole family rather than a line per case:
# phase_env writes .env.bak, .env.bak.pre-roles was made by hand during the
# §8.8 role split, and .env.deploy.bak is the one nobody has made yet. The
# named ones were each a file full of live passwords sitting one `git add -A`
# away from the history; the pattern is what stops the next one, whatever it
# gets called. Matches .env.bak, .env.bak.*, .env.deploy.bak and .env.*.bak*,
# and deliberately not .env.example, which is tracked and carries no values.
.env*.bak*
# Local-posture credentials (d.s Stage 2): source credentials AND the console
# principal registry live here. The .example.json companion IS tracked and
# carries no real values. Both are also refused by the kit's no-secrets guard
# (deploy_kit.FORBIDDEN_NAMES), so neither can ride to another machine.
.secrets.local.json
!.secrets.local.example.json

# --- Per-box rendered state (khctl regenerates these; commit the inputs, not the renders) ---
deploy_plan.json
probe_report.json
.apply_progress.json

# --- Runtime artifacts ---
operator.log
serving_usage.jsonl

# --- Python ---
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# --- Pilot corpus and client documents (data, not code) ---
pilot_sops/
reports/
